                <pb facs="0213" n="209" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg209"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.30 Asiatic Fleet/661: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Tsingtao</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sokobin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tsingtao</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-12-28T15:00:00+08:00">December 28, 1938—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 28—10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>36. Referring to the Consulate’s telegram No. 12 of November 12, 9 a.m., Standard
                    Vacuum Oil Company has reluctantly arranged for shipment of bulk gasoline from
                    Shanghai to Tsingtao on Japanese vessels one of which was permitted to discharge
                    at wharf on December 25; another Japanese vessel will bring oil to Tsingtao for
                    Company on January 1.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sokobin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
